const equivCfg = {
  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Meaning, not words', note: 'Translating words produces nonsense ("it rains cats"); translating meaning produces language. The unit of work is the message.' },
    { math: '2 · Analysis comes first', note: 'Professional translation begins by reading the source for function: what is this text doing, for whom, in what register?' },
    { math: '3 · Equivalence is a choice', note: 'Formal equivalence stays close to the source\'s shape; dynamic equivalence reproduces its effect. Neither is "the answer" — the text decides.' },
    { math: '4 · Loss is inevitable; manage it', note: 'Puns, rhythm, cultural allusion rarely survive intact. Skilled translators choose what to preserve and compensate elsewhere.' },
